**Not analysed**

- Data whose field names say nothing about it (`notes`, `payload`, `data`), free-text and JSON columns, and stores with no declared structure (key-value stores, files, schemaless collections).
- Common words left out of the bundled pattern set because they usually mean something else: `name`, `age`, `token`, `child`, `children`, `parent`, `location`, `mobile`, `health` and `minor`. A field named only one of these is not counted, so "none found" does not mean no personal data.
- Structures declared in other forms: Sequelize, Rails and other migration DSLs, GraphQL, OpenAPI and JSON Schema, schemas and migrations kept in configuration files, and generated code.
{% if sensitive.not_read %}
- Source files in languages whose structures this pass does not read (SQL in their strings was read): {% for lang, n in sensitive.not_read.items() %}{{ lang }} {{ n | fmt_int }}{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.
{% endif %}
